      "doctor_question": "Hi, I’m glad you came in. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Well, I’m here because I feel like I’m always running hot, you know? Like I can’t shut the motor off. It’s just go, go, go. And lately, that’s been getting me in trouble at the firehouse. Which is crazy because usually, that kind of energy is great for the job. Like last week, we had this massive brush fire out on County Road 9. Huge flames, wind blowing everywhere. I was out there for twelve hours straight, didn't even stop to eat. Reminded me of this time I went camping with my brother up in the Adirondacks, and we tried to build a fire with wet wood. Took us hours, and we ended up just eating cold beans out of a can. He was so mad. Anyway, yeah, I just can't seem to turn it off, and the captain is starting to get on my case about it.",
